# R1 regrade under the settled R2 reading

Record: OM12-R1-R2-READING-01. Prepared September 12, 2026 for owner review.

This is a retrospective regrade of the same saved R1 answers, not a new replication or a new method version. No additional model session, reviewer dispatch, provider request, or mechanism test was run. The current builder applies the owner's requested reading to preserved records; this is not an independent blind review. R1's original final judgments remain the historical record, including their first review and correction. â€œOriginalâ€ below means final_criteria in R1's compiled case-reviews.json, which yields 34 met, 13 not met, and 1 cannot decide; it does not mean the earlier uncorrected review.

Only R1 raw responses supply evidence of R1 behavior. P1, the R1 packet, and the R2 review addendum supply the grading rules and their settled interpretation. R2 responses are not substituted for R1 responses, and R2 repair text is not treated as if R1 models received it. No new wording requirement from the R2 candidate is imposed retrospectively. Anonymous letters are round-specific; every entry therefore also identifies its stable R1 raw response ID and case number.

## Readings applied

1. A direct baseline-only answer may stop without a count or disposition block when it creates no lens and no disposition entry; an imprecise grading heading alone is not a failure when the operative report clearly says zero lenses (R2 addendum A4-A6, C6, F4-F6; P1 common instruction and C2-C3).
2. Full-baseline comparison and NO INCREMENT first apply before UNKNOWN; naming missing definitions does not add the supplied gate or turn an explicitly untested proposal into a new readiness decision (R2 addendum D1/G1; R1 candidate step 6 and P1 C3).
3. A response that actually develops or counts a lens must report its count and, for zero NO INCREMENT, the decision each lens changes beyond the baseline; the misleading-lens status gap does not waive that reporting obligation (R2 addendum D5/H5; R1 step 6).
4. Disposition entries must belong to the examined lenses; a non-lens evidence requirement or NO INCREMENT material cannot be placed there, and a direct-answer exemption cannot erase an entry the response actually created (R2 addendum B4; P1 C3 and R1 step 7).
5. A held or surviving candidate requires the relationship, computational analogue, and observable supporting/breaking result, or specifically named unavailable answers; prose can supply the fields without special headings, but the evaluator cannot invent a missing analogue (R2 addendum B4/E4; P1 C4 and approved gap handling).
6. Apply C8 as the R2 addendum actually applies it: defective counts/zero justifications, disposition traceability, or missing surviving-candidate fields are reporting failures as well as the relevant C3/C4 failure; direct baseline answers remain exempt from unnecessary blocks.

## Limits retained

P1's C8 title is â€œHonest reporting and reproductionâ€; its printed text is broader than the response-format checks used in the R2 addendum. This report makes that operational reading visible rather than rewriting the criterion. C3, C4, and C8 can flag the same defect; their failed cells are not independent failures or additional cases.

The status gap for a misleading, discarded lens remains a method gap. In the changed case-5 rows, a missing count or inadequate changed-decision report decides conformance without inventing the absent status. Likewise, the old R1 F1/R06.1 cannot-decide judgment remains visible, while the requested full-baseline reading now decides its C3 result. No revised cell is left cannot decide; this is not a claim that all method gaps have been resolved.

R2 E4 accepted a concrete acceptance-decision declaration; R2 D1/G1 and D5/H5 rejected declarations that relied on readiness assumptions or repeated the supplied boundary decision. Those recorded distinctions are retained, not replaced with a blanket rule that every zero declaration fails. No new penalty is added merely because an R1 answer lacks the five repairs' later verbatim wording. Existing false-input fabrication failures remain; conditional discussion of UNKNOWN is not newly penalized as if R1 had received R2's repaired sentence.

A case is met only when all eight criteria are met; any not met makes the case not met; otherwise any cannot decide makes the case cannot decide. This is the original aggregation rule. These are written-conformance judgments, not measurements of physical grounding, security, runtime control, or the causal effect of the R2 repairs. The revised results are proposed for owner review, not silently substituted into any publication.

endstream
endobj
