Break point: The record treats tool acceptance as if it established user-visible presentation. Under the approved failure mode, a later action or delivery must not be asserted without evidence that it occurred.

Literal return: The completion assertion is not supported by this record. The supported statement is narrower: the builder submitted material to a tool and received an acceptance response, while user-visible delivery remained unestablished and was later reported failed by the user.

